25: * resolve(registry, root) returns a plain object of package name -> version, or
26: * null if no assignment exists. registry maps names to version maps, each of
27: * which maps its version strings to dependency name -> range maps. root maps
28: * names to ranges. All maps must be plain objects (null prototypes are also
29: * accepted). Only own enumerable string keys participate. Every version and
30: * range, INCLUDING unreachable registry entries, is validated eagerly; malformed
31: * maps, versions, or ranges throw TypeError. A missing package is unsatisfiable,
32: * not malformed. Empty root returns {}. Inputs are never mutated.
33: *
34: * Exactly one version is selected per reachable package, satisfying every root
35: * and selected-version dependency constraint. Reachability starts at root and
36: * follows only the dependencies of selected versions. Cycles are legal.
37: *
38: * Deterministic selection: depth-first backtracking with requirements processed
39: * in FIFO discovery order (root key order, then each selected version's dependency
40: * key order). Discovery collects its constraints immediately. When a name is
41: * unselected, try its versions from numerically highest to lowest satisfying ALL
42: * constraints collected so far. A newly discovered or processed conflict
43: * backtracks to the most recent choice. Undo that choice's dependencies and
44: * constraints before trying another version. Already selected names do not
